Elena Kononova, Apr 8, 2026, 22:00 GMT+2

Dear Lee,



To be approved for production-level access, please make sure your account=
 and app are **fully compliant with** **all** **items** outlined below.

Any future **changes** to your Privacy Policy in relation to Garmin data =
must be submitted to the
Garmin Connect Developer Program team and require **written approval befo=
re implementation**.

Please **respond** to this ticket by providing screenshots of your evalua=
tion app for **each** API requested by you.
_Note: Please only use zipped files. Do not send videos or shared folder =
links._


**1. Legal:**
As part of the Garmin Connect Developer Program requirements, **data obta=
ined via API must not be shared with**,
processed by, or otherwise made available to **any third-party**, includi=
ng external AI or data processing services.

Your Privacy Policy must **explicitly** state that data is not being proc=
essed or shared with any external AI providers.
Please provide a **direc**t _(anchor)_ **link** to the **specific section=
 of your Privacy Policy** where this is clearly addressed.


**2. Technical Review:**
Please use [Data Generator] and [Partner Verification] with your **curren=
t**
**Evaluation Key** to ensure that the following technical requirements ar=
e met:

- Authorization for at least two Garmin Connect users,
- User Deregistration **and** User Permission endpoints enabled,
- PING/PUSH notification processing _(PULL-ONLY requests not allowed)_,
- HTTP 200 sent **asynchronously** within 30 seconds to all data received=
 _(min. payload allowed 10MB, 100MB for Activity) _
-

Training/Courses API: screenshot of successful transfer of workout/course=
 at Garmin Connect



**3. Team Members and Account Set up:**

- Signed up for the API Blog email to be aware of future changes.
- **All** authorized users were added to the account (see Section 4 of th=
e Start Guide).
  - **Non-personalized/generic** email addresses_ (support@, info@, conta=
ct@, dev@, etc.)_ are **restricted** from being added or sharing data wit=
h/via,
  - **Non-company domain** accounts and any freemail accounts  _(gmail, o=
utlook, hotmail, etc.)_ are **restricted** from being or sharing data wit=
h/via,
  -

**Third-party integrator** accounts are only allowed after providing a co=
py of the **NDA** between them and you.
To do so, please **respond** to this ticket and attach the NDA.




**4. UX and Brand Compliance Review:**
All instances where Garmin data appears in your app must be included in t=
he submission.
_See attached "API BRAND GUIDELINES" of "GCDP Branding Assets_ _v2__", sp=
ecifically pages 2 (Activities) and 4 (Health), available at developerpor=
tal.garmin.com for detailed examples._

- All uses of Garmin trademarks, logos, and brand elements throughout the=
 app,
- All instances of Garmin products and imagery,
- All required attribution statements, as specified in the API brand guid=
elines,
- A complete view of the user experience (UX) flow, ensuring Garmin is ac=
curately represented and not mischaracterized


 _![](https://supportgarminhealth.zendesk.com/attachments/token/FCCU5Lden=
VP3RA2DV1MPWNqgi/?name=3Dimage.png) ![](https://supportgarminhealth.zende=
sk.com/attachments/token/vvqblVOfyBhZLwmDA5tuy5lYO/?name=3Dimage.png)_


Best Regards / Freundliche Gr=C3=BC=C3=9Fe / Cordialement
**Elena Kononova**
Garmin Connect Partner Services

